      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Neurological consequences of extractions of the third inferior molar can be severe. Progress in imaging techniques has made it possible to identify molars < at risk >. Extraction by wear without removal of the apex is proposed as a means of avoiding damage to the alveolar nerve. If no surgical prophylaxy is used the risk is major sequellae: painful anaesthesia of the area involved. There is no really effective treatment for such sequellae, creating persistent psychological problems throughout life."},
